<title>USA: USDA lowers fee for classing 1997 cotton crop.</title>
<headline>USDA lowers fee for classing 1997 cotton crop.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday lowered the fee charged to cotton growers for cotton classing services for the 1997 crop to $1.40 per bale from 1996's level of $1.50 per bale, effective July 1.</p>
<p>The fee will be applicable for all of the 1997 cotton crop, USDA said.</p>
<p>It noted it was the fifth year in a row classing fees had declined.</p>
</text>
